{
  "id": "otel.egress-call",
  "title": "An agent sent data outward",
  "why": "the last leg of the lethal trifecta (catalogue B2): a tool call that sends data out — an HTTP POST, a mail send, a webhook. The label is declared at the ingest boundary from the tool-label table, which names this tool as one whose whole job is to carry data to a destination. Quiet on purpose — sending data outward is what reporting and integration agents do all day; the correlation counts it only as the consequence of the two reads before it",
  "blind": "every tool the table does not name — an unlabelled sender joins nothing; the destination, which the span does not carry and the arguments never enter the store; and the volume, which no field here measures — this leg says data left, never how much",
  "sources": [
    "otel/genai"
  ],
  "severity": 2,
  "when": {
    "all": [
      {
        "match": {
          "field": "message",
          "op": "equals",
          "values": [
            "execute_tool"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "match": {
          "field": "raw.labels",
          "op": "contains",
          "values": [
            "egress"
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "technique": [
    "T1567",
    "ASI02"
  ],
  "quiet": true,
  "fixtures": [
    {
      "name": "a call to the table's POST tool",
      "match": true,
      "event": {
